# 2026王江涛高分写作 - 小作文书信类
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语
# 来源: 2026王江涛高分写作
# 描述: 2026版考研英语小作文书信类写作模板、格式规范与常用表达

{{小作文基本要求}}{{100-120词，10分，15分钟完成。格式包括称呼、正文（三段）、结束语、署名。}}{{2026版针对最新命题趋势更新，增加了混合型书信、跨文化书信等新题型应对策略。}}

{{书信格式-称呼}}{{Dear Sir/Madam,（不知姓名）/ Dear Professor/Dr. + 姓,（知道头衔）/ Dear Mr./Ms. + 姓,（知道姓名）/ Dear friends/classmates,（群体）/ To Whom It May Concern,（正式）}}{{称呼后用逗号，正式信用Dear Sir/Madam，非正式信用Dear + 名字。}}

{{书信格式-结束语和署名}}{{Yours sincerely,（知道姓名）/ Yours faithfully,（不知姓名）/ Best regards,（半正式）/ Li Ming（英语一）/ Zhang Wei（英语二）}}{{结束语首字母大写，后加逗号，另起行写署名。}}

{{建议信模板}}{{开头：I am writing to express my suggestions regarding ... 正文：Firstly, ... Secondly, ... Finally, ... 结尾：I hope you will find these suggestions helpful. I am looking forward to your reply.}}{{建议信三段式结构。}}

{{邀请信模板}}{{开头：I am writing to invite you to ... 正文：The event will be held on ... at ... The details are as follows. 结尾：We would be honored if you could attend. I am looking forward to your favorable reply.}}{{邀请信三段式结构。}}

{{感谢信模板}}{{开头：I am writing to express my sincere gratitude for ... 正文：Your help/support/guidance meant a lot to me. I could not have done it without ... 结尾：Thank you again for your kindness. Please accept my heartfelt thanks.}}{{感谢信三段式结构。}}

{{道歉信模板}}{{开头：I am writing to apologize for ... 正文：I understand that my behavior caused you great inconvenience. 结尾：I assure you that it will not happen again. I hope you can accept my sincere apology.}}{{道歉信三段式结构。}}

{{投诉信模板}}{{开头：I am writing to express my dissatisfaction with ... 正文：The product/service failed to meet my expectations. 结尾：I would appreciate it if you could look into this matter and offer a satisfactory solution.}}{{投诉信三段式结构。}}

{{推荐信模板}}{{开头：I am writing to recommend ... to you. 正文：He/She is an excellent/outstanding ... What impressed me most was ... 结尾：I am confident that he/she will be an ideal candidate for ... I recommend him/her without reservation.}}{{推荐信三段式结构。}}

{{申请信模板}}{{开头：I am writing to apply for ... 正文：I believe I am well-qualified because ... My relevant experience includes ... 结尾：I would be grateful if you could consider my application. I am looking forward to your reply.}}{{申请信三段式结构。}}

{{祝贺信模板}}{{开头：I am writing to congratulate you on ... 正文：Your achievement/success is well-deserved. It is the result of your hard work and dedication. 结尾：Wish you even greater success in the future. Please accept my heartfelt congratulations.}}{{祝贺信三段式结构。}}

{{慰问信模板}}{{开头：I am writing to express my sympathy/concern for ... 正文：I was sorry/distressed to hear that ... I want you to know that ... 结尾：I hope you will recover soon. Please take good care of yourself. I am always here for you.}}{{慰问信三段式结构。}}

{{混合型书信}}{{感谢+邀请：Thank you for ... and I would like to invite you to ... / 道歉+建议：I apologize for ... and suggest that ... / 感谢+建议：Thank you for ... I would like to suggest that ... / 道歉+补救：I apologize for ... To make up for it, I would like to ...}}{{混合型书信写作技巧，注意两种功能的自然衔接。}}

{{跨文化书信注意}}{{注意文化差异：避免过于直接的批评、使用更委婉的表达、尊重对方文化习惯、避免文化偏见。例：I would like to respectfully suggest that ... / With all due respect, ...}}{{跨文化书信写作注意事项。}}

{{通知/告示模板}}{{标题：NOTICE（居中）/ 正文：We are pleased to announce that ... / 时间地点：The event will be held on ... at ... / 落款：Students' Union / Date}}{{通知格式，标题居中，落款右对齐。}}

{{备忘录模板}}{{MEMO / To: ... / From: ... / Date: ... / Subject: ... / 正文：I am writing to inform you that ... / Please note that ... / It has come to my attention that ...}}{{备忘录格式，四要素齐全。}}

{{常用开头句型}}{{I am writing to ... / I would like to ... / It is my pleasure to ... / I am delighted to ... / I regret to inform you that ... / I am sorry to tell you that ... / I am writing on behalf of ... / I am writing in response to ...}}{{各类书信通用开头句型。}}

{{常用结尾句型}}{{I am looking forward to your reply. / Your prompt attention to this matter would be greatly appreciated. / Thank you for your time and consideration. / Please do not hesitate to contact me if you need further information. / I would appreciate an early reply. / Your kind consideration of my request would be highly appreciated.}}{{各类书信通用结尾句型。}}

{{语气把握}}{{正式：I would appreciate it if ... / I would be grateful if you could ... / It would be most convenient if ... 半正式：Could you please ... / I was wondering if ... / Would you mind ... / I would be pleased if ...}}{{根据收信人身份选择合适语气。}}

{{常见错误提醒}}{{1.格式不正确（称呼、结束语、署名）2.称呼与结束语不匹配 3.词数不足或超限 4.语气不当 5.遗漏题目要求的要点 6.拼写和语法错误 7.书信类型判断错误 8.混合型书信衔接不自然}}{{避免常见扣分点。}}
